    "stable_id": "euclid-forward-derivation",
    "canonical_statement": "For all positive integers a, b, c with a^2 + b^2 = c^2 and gcd(a,b,c) = 1, after swapping a and b if necessary there exist positive integers m > n such that gcd(m,n) = 1, m and n have opposite parity, a = m^2 - n^2, b = 2mn, and c = m^2 + n^2.",
